{"t": 1794115627.7161775, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads up: this change is causing a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue: https://us.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099), first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3 (2,201 events, unresolved).\n\nRoot cause: `int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so products that land just under a whole unit lose 1 minor unit. Fixed in worker/rates.py by rounding half up with Decimal. Commit 8c2f1d0 is flagged as the suspect commit for this issue.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
